# board.env — Sengled Smart Hub G4 (E39-G8C), contributed by @hlyi
#
# STATUS: PLACEHOLDER (v3.11.0-pre). Only BOARD_TARGET_DEVICE below is a
# verified fact — the MG13P ordering part number read off the G4 hardware
# page (PR #133). Every BOARD_UART_* value is copied verbatim from the Lidl
# reference and has NOT been confirmed on G4 hardware yet.
#
# What is verified vs. placeholder (#130):
#   - BOARD_TARGET_DEVICE: verified MG13P OPN from the #133 hardware page.
#   - BOARD_UART_FLOW=sw: established fact — the G4 has no RTS/CTS wiring (#123),
#     so it builds with software XON/XOFF flow control (paired with the bridge's
#     flow_control=sw). This is a first-class SDK option, applied by the build.
#   - BOARD_UART_PERIPHERAL / TX / RX: PLACEHOLDER, copied from the Lidl
#     reference. The OPN gives the chip, not the USART/pins this board wired —
#     the one thing still needed from @hlyi to finalize the build.
#
# CTS/RTS entries are ignored when flow=sw, kept only so the file is uniform.
#
# @hlyi: set the USART/TX/RX below to the G4 routing and validate the resulting
# NCP / OT-RCP firmware over SWD before it is trusted. See ../README.md.

BOARD_NAME="Sengled Smart Hub G4 (E39-G8C)"

# Exact MCU OPN handed to `slc generate --with` — verified from PR #133.
BOARD_TARGET_DEVICE="EFR32MG13P732F512IM32"

BOARD_UART_FLOW="sw"       # G4 has no RTS/CTS — software XON/XOFF flow (#123)

# --- PLACEHOLDER: Lidl USART/pins, pending G4 verification (#130) ---
BOARD_UART_PERIPHERAL="USART0"
BOARD_UART_PERIPHERAL_NO="0"
BOARD_UART_TX="A 0 0"      # TODO(hlyi): G4 TX pin
BOARD_UART_RX="A 1 0"      # TODO(hlyi): G4 RX pin
BOARD_UART_CTS="A 5 30"    # ignored when flow=sw
BOARD_UART_RTS="A 4 30"    # ignored when flow=sw
